From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: sendme365 <sendme365@msn.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 07:59:31 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Take a statically linked NRO payload's API names from its
 bytes

A wine-nx port's runtime NRO has no dynamic symbol table, so
romfs_nro_imports saw no imports and the guesser missed both its
Vulkan functions (taking the game for something else) and the
modules' names. When an NRO imports nothing, let the host API names
its bytes reference stand in; exports() and the nso_syms report
tolerate a game without an sdk module; and patch_nso walks .eh_frame
by hand when the image carries no binary-search table header (the
homebrew toolchain links without --eh-frame-hdr and points MOD0's
empty eh_frame_hdr range at the CIEs).

Upstream-Status: pending
Reason: wine-nx port bring-up: a statically linked runtime NRO has no dynamic table, so the profile guesser and the NSO patcher need the byte-level fallback (a PR to seedds/nxnative follows this patch)
Issue: LNPANDY/NX2Apple#1284

